  "construction": {
    "basis": "reconstruction",
    "fidelity": "not-applicable",
    "note": "The finished design was read from Wichmann’s MIR1 drawing, whose pieces are drawn edge to edge. O is the centre of a ten-pointed star whose sides are the ten lines AC, CE, … and BD, DF, …: two regular pentagons. The pattern has mirrors through the stars and half turns between them, but no half turn about a star, so it is checked by its mirror only. The repeat is a rectangle of half-sides 2 + √5 and φ/sin 36° (in OA, φ the golden ratio), with a second star on its top and bottom sides. Every line runs at an odd multiple of 18°, and every offset is (a + b√5)/20 (drawing within 0.0016 of OA). The drawing gives no steps; we devised the construction.",
    "changes": "The compass steps, their order and the named points are ours. Wichmann marks this drawing as his possible completion of a partial panel, a window shutter of the Çamlıca mosque; we build the completed pattern his drawing shows. His drawing of the shutter itself (MIR11, data213), a strip that repeats only along its length, lies exactly on our lines: every one of its edges is an edge of the completion. Colours follow the shapes. No photograph was checked.",
    "reviewed": "2026-10-27"
  },
  "credits": [
    {
      "source": "Tiling Search, data214/MIR1: Camlica Mosque, Istanbul - Completion?",
      "creator": "Brian Wichmann",
      "kind": "drawing",
      "url": "https://tilingsearch.mit.edu/HTML/data214/MIR1.html",
      "note": "Read from his finished drawing, not construction instructions. His reference is a drawing sent by Mirosław Majewski (Çamlıca mosque, Istanbul, Turkey: a possible completion)."
